"""Phase B typed adapter: MUSE (E5; NeurIPS'24) on GX / MS-v2 (RUN_NOTES_ext.md §0).

The port evalpaper/ext/MUSE/run_method.py (MUSE src @07da392, unmodified) is imported READ-ONLY. Reused as is:
load_muse, resolve_hparams (A13 §1 modal anom_0 configuration for a dataset without a released entry; modal BSize 256),
prepare_data, fit_mlp_labelfree, muse_normality, heldout_objective and muse_train (MUSE's instrumented training loop,
which calls our evaluate() at every snapshot and checkpoints through the port's maybe_stop). The port's _run is copied
below with its data part replaced (# CHANGE-TYPED):
  * container of graphs = [fit | held-out | test normals | anomalies of group 1 | group 2 | ...] (typed_data);
  * at every snapshot MUSE's error representations are computed for the whole container and the MLP autoencoder
    (h 32, lr 1e-3, 500 epochs, label-free, A13 §3) is fitted on the fit graphs, exactly as the port; the score of a
    group's test set (test normals + T) is the slice of that pass (MUSE scores every graph of its container in one
    pass by design; per graph). `--check_slice` (smoke) recomputes one group in its own container and reports the
    max |difference|;
  * the 9-cell MLP grid of the port (descriptive `oracle_grid`) is not computed; each cell is reseeded before its
    construction in the port, so the main cell is unchanged.
Own ORACLE: none (A10 §2): the collector reports UB-GOLD's rule over the 10 snapshots.
  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 $GLAD_ENVS/ubgold-gpu/bin/python -B MUSE_typed.py --generator GX --seed 0 [--fv F1]
